  "output": {
    "answer": "From the record, I write the pass/fail bar myself, before I see any output — the rule is to write the bar first, not just the gate. To keep that number honest, one experiment write-up splits the data in two: a calibration set any threshold is allowed to look at, and a separate gate set that stays untouched until the bar is frozen. It also states upfront that if a bar fails, nothing gets promoted, and that outcome can't be re-argued afterward. The excerpts don't show a second person or independent reviewer checking my bars — just this write-before-looking and split-data setup.",
